1
00:00:00,927 --> 00:00:03,307
(Leonard:)And mythological.

2
00:00:04,097 --> 00:00:05,477
(Sheldon:)Irrelevant.

3
00:00:06,307 --> 00:00:08,557
Yeah, I was studying
recombinant DNA technology...

4
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:10,816
...and I was confidant
I could create one...

5
00:00:10,979 --> 00:00:15,729
(Sheldon:)...but my parents were unwilling to secure
the necessary eagle eggs and lion semen.

6
00:00:17,735 --> 00:00:20,985
Of course, my sister got swimming lessons
when she wanted them.

7
00:00:23,408 --> 00:00:28,748
(Howard:)Sheldon, not that we don't all enjoy
a good lion-semen story...

8
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,410
...but what's your point?

9
00:00:30,581 --> 00:00:36,041
(Sheldon:)My point is, if Koothrappali is moving on
to a new life of shallow, undeserved fame...

10
00:00:36,212 --> 00:00:39,842
...then perhaps this is an opportunity
to create a better cohort.

11
00:00:40,299 --> 00:00:43,009
You wanna breed a new friend?

12
00:00:43,928 --> 00:00:46,098
(Sheldon:)That's one option, but who has the time?

13
00:00:46,764 --> 00:00:48,054
(Sheldon:)But consider this.

14
00:00:48,224 --> 00:00:51,764
(Sheldon:)The Japanese, they're doing some
wonderful work with artificial intelligence.

15
00:00:51,936 --> 00:00:56,146
Now, combine that with some animatronics
from the imagineers over at Disney.

16
00:00:56,315 --> 00:01:01,025
Next thing you know, we're playing "Halo"
with a multilingual Abraham Lincoln.

